WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.519 --> 00:00:11.940
If you would have asked me two months ago,
I would have told you it was impossible for

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.740
them to invent something more boring than
my social studies class.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.290
Turns out, I was wrong.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:22.210
Virtual social studies on a Zoom call with
Mr. Hardesty is even worse.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.590
Because with the real class I at least got
to see my best friends: Sinclair and Podge.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:31.300
In fact, the last time I saw them in person
was a month ago, the day of the protests.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.940
Ever since then, the police have been vocal
that nobody should attempt to investigate

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.870
the clown attacks on their own.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:40.560
So naturally, we had a plan to investigate
things on our own.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.650
While Mr. Hardesty was droning on about…

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:47.239
Honestly, I don’t know what, Sinclair, Podge
and I were chatting in a separate window on

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:47.880
Discord.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.700
We had a plan to get some information.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:55.120
See, while Podge and I aren’t exactly model
students, Calvin Sinclair is kind of a genius.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.100
He’d been doing some of his own research
and was filling us in on his findings.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:03.380
He explained things in our private chat: So
I started by pulling as many articles as I

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:04.240
could find.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:06.460
Creating a database of all the attacks.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:10.540
From there I mapped everything to get a visual
idea of where these incidents are happening.

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:14.200
I was hoping to find a higher concentration
somewhere, and maybe be able to determine

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.200
the source.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.049
Podge asked him if we could see his map, and
he sent over an image.

00:01:18.049 --> 00:01:20.679
I opened it up, and immediately saw the pattern!

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.860
The synapses in my brain were firing off,
and I was ready to reveal my discovery…

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.399
no of course not.

00:01:25.399 --> 00:01:27.329
I had basically no idea what I was looking
at.

00:01:27.329 --> 00:01:29.369
What do I look like, Bill Gates?

00:01:29.369 --> 00:01:33.159
As far as I could tell, it looked like there
were attacks scattered… all around the country.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:37.399
Other than the fact that bigger cities and
their suburbs seemed more likely targets,

00:01:37.399 --> 00:01:39.689
there was no real pattern that I could discern.

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:43.609
Sinclair asked us if we noticed anything about
the map, and when we had no idea, he went

00:01:43.609 --> 00:01:46.679
on to inform us he had two major takeaways
from it.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:47.880
“Excuse me!

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.360
Who is that who just joined right
now?”

00:01:50.364 --> 00:01:52.399
That was the voice of was my teacher, Mr.
Hardesty.

00:01:52.399 --> 00:01:56.090
Apparently someone had joined the call, and
he was trying to figure out who it was.

00:01:56.090 --> 00:02:00.189
The person had their camera off, and was making
a rather loud sound over the mic.

00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:04.509
It sounded like some kind of machine part,
or like a camera zooming in and out.

00:02:04.509 --> 00:02:06.130
The username was just: ARIS.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:08.679
I don’t know anyone at our school named
Aris.

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:12.380
And that was the moment I knew: we were being
eavesdropped by a clown!

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:13.640
I grabbed the nearest weapon I could find…

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:15.900
no, no of course not, it was obviously one of

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:20.010
those pranks you see online where people hack
into a video conference and create havoc.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:24.020
I had heard the security on this program is
basically non-existent, but this would have

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:26.500
been the first such intrusion that I had experienced.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:30.010
Despite thinking it was a prank, there was
something about that noise that I found kind

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:31.090
of creepy.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:33.850
Maybe this class was about to actually be
interesting!

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:38.270
However after a few minutes of nothing happening,
Aris left, and I turned my attention back

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:42.260
to our private Discord chat, where Sinclair
would explain his findings from mapping the

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.260
data.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:47.400
The first major takeaway was not what I expected:
he told us that all the attacks had taken

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.570
place in the US, meaning that the clown attacks
happening around the country were probably

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:53.600
from an American organisation.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.900
The second was more the type of observation
I’d expected him to say.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:01.320
He showed us that all the points on the map
could be connected by major highways and provided

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.290
another graphic with this linear connection
to all the affected schools.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:09.210
Not realizing I was onto something, I told
him it looked like one of those tour maps

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:13.310
you see on a band’s website, or at least
one of those tour maps you USED to see on

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:17.980
band websites before organizers started cancelling
all their tours in fear of being the future

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:19.980
targets of clown lockdowns.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:24.390
The situation had really turned from paranoia
to hysteria when the clown attacks spread

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:28.760
from just happening in classrooms to the point
they affected football games, stage plays,

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:33.030
and even school band concerts, which eventually
led any tours or concerts where kids would

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:35.390
be in attendance to be shut down.

00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:39.100
Sinclair told me he made the same connection
about the map, because of COURSE he did.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:43.130
He had already pulled data from thousands
of tours that had taken place from 2018, when

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:45.460
the attacks started to get bad, until now.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:49.860
Apparently these ticket-broker websites also
did not have the most secure information.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.970
So he was basically able to lay these tour
maps on top of our map and see which ones

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:55.069
looked similar.

00:03:55.069 --> 00:04:01.490
That narrowed our search down to 97 music
acts, 16 book tours, 7 YouTuber tour… things,

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:07.260
31 comedy shows, 4 traveling magicians…
and three… country-wide... circus tours.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:13.330
Furthermore, all three circus tours were put on by the same company: an operation by the name of Park

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:14.080
du Soleil.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:18.340
Apparently that was as much research as Sinclair
had time for, but he wanted to share that

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:19.350
with us.

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:22.740
Our obvious next step would be to look into
this Park du Soleil.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.520
I heard the garage door open.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:25.520
Must have been my dad getting home.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:29.460
I figured I’d better look like I’m paying
attention to this class when he gets in here,

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:32.650
so I minimized our Discord chat and brought
back up the Zoom lecture.

00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:38.820
“...leading some to question whether the
1975 regulations act was still effective years after...

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:40.820
Excuse me?

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:43.560
Excuse me, who is making that sound?”

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:47.629
It was the zooming sound that we’d heard
earlier -- the one that was coming from the

00:04:47.629 --> 00:04:49.110
“Aris” account.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:52.219
Only, that account was no longer in the call.

00:04:52.219 --> 00:04:56.199
I scanned through the class on my screen and
it was indicating that the sound was coming

00:04:56.199 --> 00:04:58.729
from Calvin Sinclair’s microphone.

00:04:58.729 --> 00:05:01.529
He was looking around, as if he was trying
to determine the source of the noise.

00:05:01.529 --> 00:05:05.300
Then I saw him typing, and heard the familiar
[discord sound] notification sound.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.280
I flipped back to our private chat.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.700
He was telling us he could hear that sound
in his house now, which was kind of freaking

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:11.699
him out.

00:05:11.699 --> 00:05:14.979
My Dad came into the house from the garage,
so I switched back to my class, and as I did

00:05:14.979 --> 00:05:21.500
so I noticed… someone was standing behind
Sinclair… only, it wasn’t a family member,

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.349
at least as far as I could tell.

00:05:23.349 --> 00:05:26.349
The person was wearing a yellow clown suit!

00:05:26.349 --> 00:05:31.039
Before I could say or do anything, I saw the
clown lower its head even with Sinclair’s,

00:05:31.039 --> 00:05:36.080
so that it was in the frame and we could all
see the bionic eye and robotic jawline that

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:41.409
amplified the already terrifying appearance
of the red and white face painted nightmare

00:05:41.409 --> 00:05:42.409
character!

00:05:42.409 --> 00:05:46.539
I once more heard that unsettling sound as
the bionic eye zoomed back out.

00:05:46.539 --> 00:05:50.320
Since it was now right next to my friend’s
head, it startled him -- and he jumped away from

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:54.939
it as he realized how close the intruder really
was, but in that same moment, the clown’s

00:05:54.939 --> 00:05:59.430
robotic jaw opened and emitted a purple gas
substance into my friend’s face, which he

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:02.809
immediately started choking on as he fell
out of frame.

00:06:02.809 --> 00:06:06.759
The entire class was frozen, with shocked
looks on their faces.

00:06:06.759 --> 00:06:11.089
It would have been easy for Mr. Hardesty to
chalk this up to an elaborate prank, but given

00:06:11.089 --> 00:06:15.849
the climate of recent events, he sat there,
stunned, probably not able to process what

00:06:15.849 --> 00:06:17.590
he should say or do.

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:22.199
I could feel my heart pounding in my chest
in the short moments that this all went down,

00:06:22.199 --> 00:06:25.909
but what would happen next would cause it
to sink to a place in my chest that I had

00:06:25.909 --> 00:06:27.789
never felt it before.

00:06:27.789 --> 00:06:32.379
One more time, we all heard the zoom-in sound
of the clown’s bionic eye, as it took control

00:06:32.379 --> 00:06:37.090
of Calvin’s computer and furiously typed
away, as if it were someone trying to urgently

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:39.339
write down an idea before the moment passed.

00:06:39.339 --> 00:06:42.089
His screen then glitched before going black.

00:06:42.089 --> 00:06:46.500
Seeing the look of fear on my teacher’s
face was strangely unsettling.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:50.029
Maybe it was the idea that he’s supposed
to be an authority figure and he’s supposed

00:06:50.029 --> 00:06:53.620
to know what to do when something bad happens
-- and he didn’t.

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:58.900
Or maybe it was the fact that we were no longer
safe anywhere -- even inside of our own homes.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:02.229
Either way, I can never forget that look he
had.

00:07:02.229 --> 00:07:06.339
The rest of the class was cancelled, and Podge
and I desperately tried to contact Sinclair

00:07:06.339 --> 00:07:07.810
to see if he was OK.

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:10.619
We mulled over the idea of showing up to get
answers.

00:07:10.619 --> 00:07:14.550
The police had obviously been called, so it
seemed like a safe place to be, but I think

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:16.249
we both feared for the worst.

00:07:16.249 --> 00:07:20.619
We had just about decided on a plan when I
heard something that made me freeze.

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.160
*zoom*

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:28.119
I slowly turned in horror to see that there
was someone standing AT MY WINDOW.

00:07:28.119 --> 00:07:33.029
The same clown that had attacked Sinclair
30 minutes ago was now coming after me.

00:07:33.029 --> 00:07:36.069
My head spun and my insides did somersaults.

00:07:36.069 --> 00:07:37.999
I realized what must have happened.

00:07:37.999 --> 00:07:41.119
It was somehow using the computers to find
us in real life.

00:07:41.119 --> 00:07:43.999
It started when “Aris” had joined in the
Zoom call.

00:07:43.999 --> 00:07:48.370
That’s when it found Sinclair’s location,
then it used his computer to get to the next

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:50.410
in line, which may have been me.

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:53.490
Or maybe there was one before me -- who knows
at this point.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:56.809
In a panic, I fumbled my way out of my chair,
knocking it over as I did so.

00:07:56.809 --> 00:08:00.960
I didn’t turn my back on the cyberclown,
which caused me to go full-horror movie protagonist

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:03.680
and slip and stumble my way away from the
window.

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:07.000
But it was also the reason that I was looking
in that direction when…

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:07.500
*CRACK*

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:11.820
Something lashed out from outside the window
frame and struck the clown around it’s left

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:13.680
eye, the non-bionic one.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:17.180
The clown let out an inhuman scream and fell
to the ground.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:20.700
That’s when I saw my Dad, wielding an old
hockey stick from the garage.

00:08:20.719 --> 00:08:22.800
He whacked the clown several times on the
ground.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:27.060
On the third hit, the stick seem to get caught
on something and stuck in place.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:31.380
He tried to pull it back, and finally pulled it
hard enough for the blade to break away from the

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:32.100
handle.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:36.920
We would later find the blade totally deformed
in the yard, as if it were a chewed up toothpick.

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:42.039
My Dad came back inside and locked us in the
basement as he called the police.

00:08:42.039 --> 00:08:43.590
We didn’t see the cyberclown again.

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:48.210
The police showed up, collected the evidence,
and that was about it, as they were probably

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:50.980
off to make a report of the next clown attack.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:53.820
I tried to listen in during the short time
they were there.

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:57.780
One of them mentioned something about the
mayor planning to issue a mandatory stay-at-home

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:02.100
order for all kids -- and how that idea wasn’t
going to do much good if the attacks are now

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:04.590
happening in residential neighborhoods…

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:06.950
We never found out what happened to Sinclair.

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:08.160
He’s STILL missing.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.780
Things have only gotten worse.

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:12.520
I talked to Podge again tonight.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:17.030
He too, was shaken, but we both agreed that
the police weren’t doing enough.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:20.680
We wanted to continue the investigation that
Sinclair started.

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:24.340
And that began with looking into this circus:
Park du Soleil.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:28.560
We found out it was started in the mid 2000s
by a guy named Otis Park.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:31.510
So that’s where our search would have to
begin.

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:34.340
I haven’t seen another clown since that
day.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:37.160
But sometimes, in the dead of the night,

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.900
I still think I hear that sound.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.720
*zooooom*

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:44.940
*click*

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:49.680
Thanks for listening to Al Dente Creepypasta.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:54.500
Your total today comes out to $19.75 but if
you like this video right now I’ll waive

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:58.690
that fee and give you everything you just
listened to absolutely free.

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:03.840
Remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, RING that deathbell for

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:07.070
notifications and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:10.340
Assuming we both survive.

